material></sec></body><back><ack><sec><title>Acknowledgment</title><p>The authors thank IMPACC for sharing tracheal aspirate sequencing data from subjects coenrolled in the COMET and IMPACC studies.</p></sec></ack><fn-group><fn fn-type="supported-by"><p>Supported by National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute grants F32HL151117 (A.S.), K23HL163491 (A.S.), R35HL140026 (C.S.C.), 5K24HL133390 (C.S.C.), and 5R01HL155418 (C.R.L.); National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases grant U19AI1077439 (D.J.E. and C.S.C.); University of California San Francisco Bakar ImmunoX Initiative; University of California San Francisco Strategic Initiative Funding for the CoLabs Initiative; Chan Zuckerberg Initiative; and Genentech grant TSK-020586.</p></fn><fn><p>Author Contributions: Conceptualization: A.S., S.A.C., and C.S.C. Formal analysis/software: A.S., S.A.C., A.P.O., L.P.A.N., E.M., M.V.M., S.H.C., A.B., and K.L.K. Data curation: H.Z., A.J., R.G., S.C., and T.D. Investigation: A.S., B.Z.S., P.S., J.G.W., F.M., A.L., E.R.S., Z.M.L., R.G., S.C., P.S.H., T.D., C.L., K.N.K., C.M.H., M.A.M., C.R.L., L.D.J.B., and C.S.C. Visualization: A.S. Funding acquisition: A.S., C.R.L., D.J.E., and C.S.C. Project administration: J.L.D., D.J.E., M.F.K., K.N.K., C.M.H., P.G.W., M.A.M., C.R.L., and C.S.C. Supervision: S.A.C., C.R.L., and C.S.C. Writing &#x02013; original draft: A.S. Writing &#x02013; review &#x00026; editing: all authors.</p></fn><fn><p>Data and materials availability: Code for differential expression and single-cell RNA sequencing analyses is available at <ext-link xlink:href="https://github.com/AartikSarma/ARDSPhenotypes" ext-link-type="uri">https://github.com/AartikSarma/ARDSPhenotypes</ext-link>. The processed gene count data are available from the National Center for Biotechnology Information Gene Expression Omnibus database under accession code GSE200849. The raw sequencing data used in this analysis are protected because of data privacy restrictions from the institutional review board protocols governing patient enrollment in this study, which protect the release of raw genetic sequencing data from those patients enrolled under a waiver of consent. Researchers who wish to obtain raw FASTQ files for the purposes of independently generating gene counts can contact the corresponding author (<email xlink:href="mailto:aartik.sarma@ucsf.edu">aartik.sarma@ucsf.edu</email>) to be added to the institutional review board protocols and sign a materials transfer agreement from the University of California San Francisco ensuring that the data will be securely stored and only used for transcriptomic analyses.</p></fn><fn><p><ext-link xlink:href="https://doi.org/10.1164/rccm.202504-0784ED" ext-link-type="uri">This article has a related editorial</ext-link>.</p></fn><fn><p>A data supplement for this article is available via the <ext-link xlink:href="http://www.atsjournals.org/doi/suppl/10.1164/rccm.202407-1454OC?role=tab" ext-link-type="uri">Supplements tab</ext-link> at the top of the online article.</p></fn><fn><p>Artificial Intelligence Disclaimer: No artificial intelligence tools were used in writing this manuscript.</p></fn><fn><p>Originally Published in Press as DOI: <ext-link xlink:href="https://doi.org/10.1164/rccm.202407-1454OC" ext-link-type="uri">10.1164/rccm.202407-1454OC</ext-link> on September 25, 2025</p></fn><fn fn-type="financial-disclosure"><p><underline><bold><ext-link xlink:href="http://www.atsjournals.org/doi/suppl/10.1164/rccm.202407-1454OC/suppl_file/disclosures.pdf" ext-link-type="uri">Author disclosures</ext-link></bold></underline> are available with the text of this article at <ext-link xlink:href="http://www.atsjournals.org" ext-link-type="uri">www.atsjournals.org</ext-link>.</p></fn></fn-group><ref-list><title>References</title><ref id="bib1"><label>1.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal">
